@quotation
@strong{@anchor{Exercise 5.19}Exercise 5.19:} Alyssa P. Hacker wants a
@newterm{breakpoint} feature in the simulator to help her debug her machine
designs.  You have been hired to install this feature for her.  She wants to be
able to specify a place in the controller sequence where the simulator will
stop and allow her to examine the state of the machine.  You are to implement a
procedure

@example kotlin
machine.setBreakpoint(@var{label}, @var{n})
@end example

@noindent
that sets a breakpoint just before the @math{n^{\hbox{th}}} instruction after the given
label.  For example,

@example kotlin
gcdMachine.setBreakpoint("test-b", 4)
@end example

@noindent
installs a breakpoint in @code{gcd-machine} just before the assignment to
register @code{a}.  When the simulator reaches the breakpoint it should print
the label and the offset of the breakpoint and stop executing instructions.
Alyssa can then use @code{reg(name).content} reads and writes to manipulate
the state of the simulated machine.
She should then be able to continue execution by calling @code{step}
until the machine is halted.

@noindent
She should also be able to remove a specific breakpoint or all breakpoints
by clearing the parked-machine table the exercise keeps beside the machine.
@end quotation
